    "latencyTargetMs": 500,
    "costBudget": 1800
  },
  "explanation": [
    "RAG grounds answers in your documents: embed the question, find the nearest document chunks in a vector index, and put them in the prompt.",
    "Model latency dominates, so streaming matters: users see the first tokens in a few hundred ms instead of waiting for the whole answer.",
    "Rate limits are a capacity limit. Near the limit, requests queue and latency explodes, so plan headroom with more deployments, a faster model, or caching common answers.",
    "Model choice is a latency/quality/cost trade-off: a fast model (Groq-hosted) cuts latency sharply, and a larger model may answer better."
  ]
